From: hashtagbasit
Subject: Input: goodix: keep the DT size when the config is invalid

When the config read back from the chip is unusable, the driver falls back
to 4096x4096 for the touch area, even when touchscreen-size-x/-y in the
device tree already said how big it is. The AYANEO Pocket S 2K's GT911
returns a garbled config (no contact count), so its 1440x2560 coordinates
were scaled as if they spanned 4096 and every touch landed in the wrong
place. Only fall back for the sizes the device tree didn't give.

diff -ru a/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c
@@ -1232,8 +1232,15 @@
 		dev_err(&ts->client->dev,
 			"Invalid config (%d, %d, %d), using defaults\n",
 			ts->prop.max_x, ts->prop.max_y, ts->max_touch_num);
-		ts->prop.max_x = GOODIX_MAX_WIDTH - 1;
-		ts->prop.max_y = GOODIX_MAX_HEIGHT - 1;
+		/*
+		 * Keep a size the device tree gave: only the contact count may
+		 * be missing (a garbled config), and the chip still reports
+		 * in panel coordinates.
+		 */
+		if (!ts->prop.max_x)
+			ts->prop.max_x = GOODIX_MAX_WIDTH - 1;
+		if (!ts->prop.max_y)
+			ts->prop.max_y = GOODIX_MAX_HEIGHT - 1;
 		ts->max_touch_num = GOODIX_MAX_CONTACTS;
 		input_abs_set_max(ts->input_dev,
 				  ABS_MT_POSITION_X, ts->prop.max_x);
